        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A premium visual breakdown of how a £60 injector tip failure destroyed a £4,000+ OM651 engine, and why a reconditioned engine with 3-day downtime was the smart business decision."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "“The driver called me on a Tuesday morning. He said, ‘Boss, the van just started sounding like a bag of hammers. White smoke everywhere. I’ve pulled over.’ By Wednesday lunchtime, the specialist called with the news — an injector tip had snapped off inside cylinder three. It had bounced around, destroyed the piston, wrecked the head, and scored the bore. The engine was scrap. I needed that van back on the road by Friday or I’d lose a £3,000 contract.”"
        },
